      "id": "KUKULCAN.SharedKernel",
      "range": "*"
    },
    "message": "It has been developed from scratch, to eliminate dependencies on third-party libraries. \n.- Added common domain primitives and abstractions. \n.- Added Result and Result<T> handling. \n.- Added standardized errors and error codes. \n.- Added validation infrastructure and validation extensions. \n.- Added time abstractions and clock implementations. \n.- Added value-object and structural comparison utilities. \n.- Added common messages and cross-cutting components. \n.- Included XML documentation for the public API. \n.- Designed as a reusable foundation for KUKULCAN applications and services.",
    "reasons": [
      "Other",
      "Legacy",
      "CriticalBugs"
    ]
  },
  "description": "KUKULCAN.Kernel is the cross-cutting core of the ATLAS ecosystem.\nIt defines the domain primitives, infrastructure contracts, extensions, and MediatR pipeline behaviors that every module, and immutable components that ensure consistency, interoperability, and stability across all bounded contexts and services.",
